{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts","id":486901,"title":"pentex subsidaries closest real life counterparts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-20T18:12:28-07:00","id":486901,"title":"pentex subsidaries closest real life counterparts","content":"I'm running a game involving pentex and would prefer to run the pentex subsidiaries as their real world counterparts because everyone automatically suspects endron, otolleys etc.<br /> <br /> Looking for input on a few or suggestions if you think another company fits better.<br /> <br /> Endron - Exxon Mobil<br /> O'Tolleys- McDonald's<br /> King Breweries- Budweiser/ annheisher Busch<br /> magadon - ???<br /> Sunburst - Google, Apple or Microsoft?<br /> RED Network - FOX<br /> Tellus Games - EA or Activision?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T18:32:53-07:00","id":486937,"title":"","content":"wasn't there a pentex subsidiary that was a parody of whitewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T18:38:40-07:00","id":486941,"title":"","content":"Black dog, but that counterpart is obvious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T19:16:32-07:00","id":486964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=486941#post486941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black dog, but that counterpart is obvious</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually just use Wizard of the Coast, since it's one of the bigger (maybe biggest) RPG companies<br /> <br /> For Magadon:<br /> Quote from a Google search for &quot;largest pharmaceutical company in new jersey&quot;:<br /> The State is home to 14 of the world's 20 largest pharmaceutical companies, including <b>Novartis</b>, <b>Johnson &amp; Johnson</b>, Bristol-Myers Squibb, <b>Merck &amp; Co</b>., Novo Nordisk and <b>Bayer Healthcare</b>. Furthermore, New Jersey boasts a well-educated workforce with a high concentration of scientific professionals.<br /> <br /> Pick one. Apparently NJ has very appealing tax laws and other incentives for pharmaceutical companies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T19:56:44-07:00","id":486972,"title":"","content":"While some of the subsidiaries are clearly meant to be parodies of a well known company, I think a lot are generic parodies of certain industries as a whole. Circinius Brands is named as a play off the word carcinogen, an agent which causes cancer. Magadon is named after one of the trade names of the drug Nitrazepam. Also, some of the companies that served as inspirations are gone now \u2013 either bankrupt or bought out by another corporation \u2013 or no longer as dominant. Anheuser Busch, which produces Budweiser -the \u201cKing of Beers\u201d, is clearly the model for King Breweries. However, Budweiser is now owned by ABInbev nased out of Belgium. Vesuvius Incorporated was a publisher of a wide range of books, comics, and periodicals \u2013 yet the only large companies that pritned comic books in the 1990s \u2013 Marvel, DC (as a branch of Warner Brothers), Image, and Dark Horse don't fit that description at all. They either published solely comics or was part of a huge media conglomerate with TV, movies, and music. Young and Smith makes both food and personal care products, but I don't know of any company which produces both \u2013 so which industry do you use? The writers were also US based, and there is a very strong US bias even when the industries in question (like mining) are more likely to be foreign.<br /> Thus, different people are going to come up with different lists.<br /> While you may want to use well known names for some of these companies, you may want to come up with some of your own names. Here is one list using some big name companies as stand ins.<ul><li>Ardus Enterprises - Waste Management, Inc.</li> <li>Autumn Health Management Systems - Health Management Associates</li> <li>Avalon Incorporated - Hasbro</li> <li>Black Dog Game Factory - White Wolf</li> <li>Circinus Brands - Altria</li> <li>Consolidex Worldwide - Morgan Stanley</li> <li>Endron International - ExxonMobil</li> <li>Good House International - Kimberly-Clark</li> <li>Hallahan Fishing Company - Trident Seafoods</li> <li>Harold and Harold Mining, Incorporated - Glencore</li> <li>Herculean Firearms Incorporated - Smith &amp; Wesson</li> <li>Herrick's - Wal-Mart</li> <li>King Breweries and Distillers - Anheuser Busch Inbev</li> <li>Magadon, Incorporated - Merck Pharmaceuticals</li> <li>Nastrum Enterprises - Lockheed Martin</li> <li>Omni Television - The CW</li> <li>O'Tolley's: &quot;The Family Place&quot; - McDonalds</li> <li>Rainbow Incorporated - Rubbermaid</li> <li>Tellus Enterprises - Nintendo</li> <li>Sunburst Enterprises International - Microsoft</li> <li>Vesuvius Incorporated - Warner Brothers</li> <li>Young and Smith, Incorporated - Procter &amp; Gamble plus Kraft Foods</li> </ul>Personally, I do not like the depiction of Pentex in the game for multiple reasons. The companies are far too big and well known to make effective Wyrm fronts. I'd prefer much smaller companies mostly privately owned, but in effective niche markets or second tier suppliers to the big boys. Why be McDonalds when you can be one of the nameless beef suppliers to them and the other fast food chains?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T20:10:13-07:00","id":486975,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>King Breweries and Distillers - Anheuser Busch Inbev<br /> <br /> The ultra-conservative King family is also clearly a Coors reference</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T21:11:13-07:00","id":487005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=486975#post486975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>King Breweries and Distillers - Anheuser Busch Inbev<br /> <br /> The ultra-conservative King family is also clearly a Coors reference</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Budweiser Frogs get bossed by Coors alligator:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JoI911uawTU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JoI911uawTU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JoI911uawTU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JoI911uawTU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T21:55:44-07:00","id":487041,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.kochindustriesinc.com/Companies/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.kochindustriesinc.com/Companies/</a> here's a good list but it might be bit on the nose....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T23:21:21-07:00","id":487067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=486975#post486975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[LIST]The ultra-conservative King family is also clearly a Coors reference</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call.<br /> <br /> It just goes to show there is no one to one relationship. It's various rifts on the culture.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T08:06:10-07:00","id":487293,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. Thanks for the list black fox","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:54:24-07:00","id":489530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=486972#post486972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST]Personally, I do not like the depiction of Pentex in the game for multiple reasons. The companies are far too big and well known to make effective Wyrm fronts. I'd prefer much smaller companies mostly privately owned, but in effective niche markets or second tier suppliers to the big boys. Why be McDonalds when you can be one of the nameless beef suppliers to them and the other fast food chains?</div> </div> </div> </div>A good example of this is when Nestle recalled some Hot Pockets last year; Nestle didn't even deal directly with the company that was the source of the tainted beef (Rancho Feeding). You could get all sorts of horrid things into the supply chain with no one having a clue who you were.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to see what a more business saavy version of Pentex (or rather, Pentex's numerous successors) looked like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5773-peat","name":"Peat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T10:54:12-07:00","id":489647,"title":"","content":"The online-game setting I'm working on has packs 'adopting' small wyrm-tainted companies and minor villains, so there's always someone to go after even when there aren't big sept-spanning plots going on at the moment, and they're generally things exactly like Peat said...local producers, &quot;unaffiliated&quot; mining operations, tainted hospitals. Something big enough that a pack can't (or won't want to) just wipe it off the map in a flash of violent ecoterrorism, but small enough that you just might run into the guys in charge. Also the guys who are actually in charge of the wyrm stuff at that operation, which is probably someone different that the figurehead might not even know about.<br /> <br /> Fighting a monolithic corporation of evil and never being able to make much of a difference can be thematic but it's not all that interesting. It's fun letting a pack or two take on a corporate entity and actually win long-term for once.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's no reason these small fry can't coexist with Pentex itself. Are they secretly still working for Pentex, or are they working alone--and which answer is the biggest conspiracy? Is there something back in Malfeas pulling all the strings at once, or does the right hand not know what the left is doing...if you pit these corporations against each other, is it a good thing, or are you still playing into their hands? Such are the conversations of drunk Galliards, depressed Theurges, and Ragabashes in tinfoil hats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T23:09:56-07:00","id":490244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=489647#post489647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such are the conversations of drunk Galliards, depressed Theurges, and Ragabashes in tinfoil hats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Ragabash stopped wearing the tinfoil hats because they kept getting ripped apart every time they shifted to Crinos. (The hats got ripped apart, not the Ragabash.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T23:16:42-07:00","id":490251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=490244#post490244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the Ragabash stopped wearing the tinfoil hats because they kept getting ripped apart every time they shifted to Crinos. (The hats got ripped apart, not the Ragabash.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The cautionary note reminds me of changing forms in an un-detected suit of armor in Werewolf the Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T23:22:46-07:00","id":490255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=490251#post490251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The cautionary note reminds me of changing forms in an un-detected suit of armor in Werewolf the Dark Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Undetected? As in &quot;it's kind of hard to sneak around while wearing plate armor, never mind if you're in Homid form or, Gaia forfend, wearing plate armor in Crinos form?&quot; Or did you mean &quot;un-Dedicated,&quot; meaning the armor won't change forms with the Garou wearing it because it hadn't had the Rite of Dedication performed on it?<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you meant un-Dedicated, that would get a bit...<i>messy</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T07:10:48-07:00","id":490500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=490255#post490255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Undetected? As in &quot;it's kind of hard to sneak around while wearing plate armor, never mind if you're in Homid form or, Gaia forfend, wearing plate armor in Crinos form?&quot; Or did you mean &quot;un-Dedicated,&quot; meaning the armor won't change forms with the Garou wearing it because it hadn't had the Rite of Dedication performed on it?<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you meant un-Dedicated, that would get a bit...<i>messy</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It was late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T08:13:18-07:00","id":490582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=490255#post490255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Undetected? As in &quot;it's kind of hard to sneak around while wearing plate armor, never mind if you're in Homid form or, Gaia forfend, wearing plate armor in Crinos form?&quot; Or did you mean &quot;un-Dedicated,&quot; meaning the armor won't change forms with the Garou wearing it because it hadn't had the Rite of Dedication performed on it?<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you meant un-Dedicated, that would get a bit...<i>messy</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Potentially usefully messy, if your GM is kind enough to rule that going from Homid to Crinos basically shatters the armour from the inside, causing sharp metal fragments to go flying off and creating a shrapnel effect...<br /> <br /> <br /> Might be a bit far fetched though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5773-peat","name":"Peat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T14:21:15-07:00","id":490917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=490582#post490582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Potentially usefully messy, if your GM is kind enough to rule that going from Homid to Crinos basically shatters the armour from the inside, causing sharp metal fragments to go flying off and creating a shrapnel effect...<br /> <br /> Might be a bit far fetched though.</div> </div> </div> </div>So essentially the medieval version of a suicide vest?...<i>Yuck</i>.<br /> <br /> Actually, no, that wouldn't even work. Plate armor is made of several pieces held in place over the body by leather straps. The straps would snap long before the metal would crack if a Garou shifted to Crinos while wearing the non-Dedicated armor. The armor wouldn't even fly off the Garou's body; the separate pieces of the armor would just fall off his chest, arms and legs as the leather straps ripped.<br /> <br /> Chain mail, being made of a bunch of linked metal pieces, however....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T15:35:35-07:00","id":490997,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I imagine the Garou never really cared for chain shirts or chain swathing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T15:57:59-07:00","id":491028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=490582#post490582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Potentially usefully messy, if your GM is kind enough to rule that going from Homid to Crinos basically shatters the armour from the inside, causing sharp metal fragments to go flying off and creating a shrapnel effect...<br /> <br /> <br /> Might be a bit far fetched though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish that were a Gift. Assuming that it didn't damage the user, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:34:31-07:00","id":491621,"title":"","content":"As I said, it would be a bit far fetched and require a GM firmly on your side. Deffo makes more sense as chain mail. Not sure it would even hurt the Garou - the metal's going away from you and even if it does hit you, you're now in Crinos and probably not that bothered. I think I'd make it a gift though, rather than just a standard thing.<br /> <br /> edit: Or, if not on your side, on the side of general destruction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5773-peat","name":"Peat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T13:02:25-07:00","id":492835,"title":"","content":"Pentex = Pentex Energies Inc.? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.interiorgas.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/IGU_Logo_horizontal-updated-web.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/\" target=\"_blank\"> Lawmakers express concern over AIDEA&rsquo;s proposed purchase of Pentex Alaska </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Alan Bailey,&nbsp;Petroleum News Some lawmakers in the Alaska Legislature have voiced concerns over the proposal by the Alaska Industrial Development and Export Authority to purchase Pentex Alaska Natural Gas Co. LLC, the owner company of Fairbanks Natural Gas, of a small liquefied natural gas plant at Point MacKenzie on Cook Inlet and of the trucking operation </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Apparently Pentex was founded in 2006... but, still... A little concerning when RL imitates fiction. :-/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T17:30:05-07:00","id":494116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=492835#post492835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex = Pentex Energies Inc.? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers...pentex-alaska/</a><br /> <br /> Apparently Pentex was founded in 2006... but, still... A little concerning when RL imitates fiction. :-/</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an older friend who is former navy intelligence who once told me that most of the US's nukes during the cold war were made by a plant called Pantex , just one letter different but still in a wyrmish area. Apparently it's also a brand of cameras.<br /> <br /> Of course there is also a biotech company in real life that has the same name as the evil biotech company from NWoD hunter, so I'm just gonna chalk up to what I call the <i>Simpsons effect</i> &quot;Any fiction series that runs long enough will eventually touch on something in real life that the writers didn't know about, even if the something in real life hadn't happened yet when the work was made.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 04-27-2015, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T18:46:54-07:00","id":494200,"title":"","content":"My first manual camera back in school was a Pentax (also one letter off) K-1000. The choice camera for students at that time because they were virtually indestructible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T06:50:22-07:00","id":1257953,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm a little late but still...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=492835#post492835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex = Pentex Energies Inc.? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.interiorgas.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/IGU_Logo_horizontal-updated-web.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/\" target=\"_blank\"> Lawmakers express concern over AIDEA&rsquo;s proposed purchase of Pentex Alaska </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.interiorgas.com/lawmakers-express-concern-aideas-proposed-purchase-pentex-alaska/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Alan Bailey,&nbsp;Petroleum News Some lawmakers in the Alaska Legislature have voiced concerns over the proposal by the Alaska Industrial Development and Export Authority to purchase Pentex Alaska Natural Gas Co. LLC, the owner company of Fairbanks Natural Gas, of a small liquefied natural gas plant at Point MacKenzie on Cook Inlet and of the trucking operation </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Apparently Pentex was founded in 2006... but, still... A little concerning when RL imitates fiction. :-/</div> </div> </div> </div>The funniest thing is that Pentex started as Premium Oil, a company that mined gas also <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Another example of Pentex perfidity:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.indiedb.com/games/tellus-save-the-earth\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.indiedb.com/games/tellus-save-the-earth</a><br /> <br /> I also plan to run a campaign in which my players will try to ruin some of Pentex plans (something like Monkeywrench Pentex supplement). They (the players) are almost virgins in terms of W:tA world and glossary so they will be surprised. I am looking for some ideas involving humans (some kind of veiled evil corporate plans), not some kind of monster slaying actions. Something that will make my players wonder is it truly BSD they should be worry. I am also willing to share some of my ideas. But please send me yours as private messages not posts. I believe that some of them are here and I don't want to spoil the surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T22:41:35-07:00","id":1258332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=486972#post486972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...[*]Endron International - ExxonMobil<br /> ...[*]Herculean Firearms Incorporated - Smith &amp; Wesson<br /> ...[*]Herrick's - Wal-Mart<br /> ...[*]King Breweries and Distillers - Anheuser Busch InBev<br /> ...[*]Nastrum Enterprises - Lockheed Martin[*]O'Tolley's: &quot;The Family Place&quot; - McDonalds[*]Sunburst Enterprises International - Microsoft[*]Vesuvius Incorporated - Warner Brothers[*]Young and Smith, Incorporated - Procter &amp; Gamble plus Kraft Foods<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Endron / ExxonMobil<br /> Disagree. Exxon (and by extension MobilOil) actually learned somewhat from the <i>Exxon Valdez</i> disaster. They're not squeaky clean, but they're hardly the worst offender. BP on the other hand is <i>notorious</i> for some of the environmental and safety sh** they do. Their corporate culture is very much aligned to the ideal that the fine is always cheaper than compliance. But my #1 for Endron would be Haliburton and their various thinly-veiled spin-offs like Kellogg Brown &amp; Root.<br /> <br /> Herculean Firearms / Smith &amp; Wesson.<br /> Too big. Too legit. I'd go with Taurus. Smaller. Focuses on the psycho-gun-nut crowd more. Specializes in cheap, Saturday night special .22LR crap. Also, given the names, I suspect that's what White Wolf's writers actually had in mind.<br /> <br /> Herrick's / Wal-Mart<br /> Meh... I'd actually associate Wal-Mart more with StarMart (the Weaver-controlled company)<br /> <br /> King / Anheuser Busch<br /> Only, it's actually explicitly stated that King is a smaller competitor to Anheuser Busch (and Miller, Coors, etc.)<br /> <br /> All the others are simply too big. Pentex is big, but their subsidiaries are never the #1 (or #2, or #3). They like to hide themselves a little further down the totem pole. Particularly since, if they do something, they can persuade their larger competitors to follow suit to &quot;stay competitive&quot;. Also, I've always sort of assumed that Sunburst was a tongue-in-cheek reference to Sun Microsystems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T20:28:27-07:00","id":1258483,"title":"","content":"As I explained in that post from three years ago:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=486972#post486972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While some of the subsidiaries are clearly meant to be parodies of a well known company, I think a lot are generic parodies of certain industries as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=486972#post486972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you may want to use well known names for some of these companies, you may want to come up with some of your own names. Here is one list using some big name companies as stand ins.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I don't know what the point of your comment is. The original poster wanted some real names he could use in place of the PENTEX ones. So I gave him some. If you want to give other options three years afterwards, you're free to do so. How closely did you actually read the thread?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T19:01:32-07:00","id":1258640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=1258332#post1258332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Herculean Firearms / Smith &amp; Wesson.<br /> Too big. Too legit. I'd go with Taurus. Smaller. <b>Focuses on the psycho-gun-nut crowd more</b>. Specializes in cheap, Saturday night special .22LR crap. </div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. As a &quot;psycho gun nut&quot; myself, Smith and Wesson favors my crowd far, FAR more heavily than Taurus. And while Taurus makes some cheap weapons, they have risen quite a bit in quality over the years--especially their revolvers, for which they are now mostly known for. Meanwhile, S&amp;W regularly send me emails to remind me to be a &quot;patriot&quot; and purchase more of their firearms.<br /> <br /> Ruger, Beretta, or Springfield might be more accurate in terms of scale.<br /> <br /> To be fair, however, I doubt many White Wolf employees were gun afficionados at the time that Pentex was originally written. Especially guys like Phil Brucato who's not a fan of them. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T03:43:49-07:00","id":1258693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts#post486901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a game involving pentex and would prefer to run the pentex subsidiaries as their real world counterparts because everyone automatically suspects endron, otolleys etc.<br /> <br /> Looking for input on a few or suggestions if you think another company fits better.<br /> <br /> Endron - Exxon Mobil<br /> O'Tolleys- McDonald's<br /> King Breweries- Budweiser/ annheisher Busch<br /> magadon - ???<br /> Sunburst - Google, Apple or Microsoft?<br /> RED Network - FOX<br /> Tellus Games - EA or Activision?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try maybe look from another angle: as far as I remember 99% of p. ex. Magadon products are real pharmaceutics. The only side effect is that they increase Wyrm aura in users so real Wyrm minions becomes more difficult to detect. If Pentex subsidiaries products were too tainted prople would stop using them. My advice: don't try to find real life counterparts. Rather make the characters chase their own tails. For example create some news about Pentex subsidiaries (Magadon creates new tranquilizer, new gas from Endron help you keep yours car's engine clan etc). It should be normal, untainted products. And among them put a few news about products that are real threat. Because if we talk about Pentex subsidiaries the 2 main problems are that they are indispensable for life and the real threat is hidden in plain sight.<br /> <br /> Or you can also hide Pentex intrigues among other corporations. Imagine that: BP oil well from Mexican Gulf was destroyed by rokea (they mistook it for Endron well; I doubt that they dam tell the difference). Or BP copied Endron politics. Or it was just an accident... How the player's characters could tell the difference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-03-2018, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T01:07:26-07:00","id":1258839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=1258693#post1258693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can also hide Pentex intrigues among other corporations. Imagine that: BP oil well from Mexican Gulf was destroyed by rokea (they mistook it for Endron well; I doubt that they dam tell the difference). Or BP copied Endron politics. Or it was just an accident... How the player's characters could tell the difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem... OR it actually WAS Pentex. Keep in mind that back in the real world, while BP owned the well -- it was an outfit called Transocean that was subcontracted to drill it and owned the rig. In the World of Darkness, there's nothing to say that entirely legit corporations like BP don't wind up subcontracting out to veiled tendrils of Endron or some other Pentex subsidiary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T02:23:38-07:00","id":1258844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/486901-pentex-subsidaries-closest-real-life-counterparts?p=1258839#post1258839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahem... OR it actually WAS Pentex. Keep in mind that back in the real world, while BP owned the well -- it was an outfit called Transocean that was subcontracted to drill it and owned the rig. In the World of Darkness, there's nothing to say that entirely legit corporations like BP don't wind up subcontracting out to veiled tendrils of Endron or some other Pentex subsidiary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's another option. But you got the point. The thing imho is that Pentex rarely could be connected to harmful activities directly. I think that it would rather give people something absolutely harmless and rely on human stupidity. Or creativity, whatever you want to call it. As with knife: you could prepare your meal with it or kill somebody (if knife was made by Pentex it could be the same :P). Or bend the law. Breaking it is the last and rarely used option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}